  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 256 AM EDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\n- Mostly Fair Weather through the Weekend\n\nHigh pressure moves in today with lower humidity. The drying\npersists into Saturday when the high moves east and return flow\nbrings some moisture. There could be a few showers Saturday night\ninto Sunday, but current dry forecast will not be changed until \nthere is more ensemble support for deeper moisture.\n\n- Showers and Thunderstorms Possible Late Monday into Tuesday\n\nA shortwave trough ejects out of the northern Rockies with a\nsurface low tracking into Canada early next week. A trailing cold\nfront is expected to touch off showers and thunderstorms by late\nMonday into Tuesday. Instability and deeper moisture is across\nnorthern Lower Michigan pooling ahead of the cold front, which\nsinks south through the forecast area on Tuesday. Precipitable\nwater surges over 2 inches, so heavy rain potential is there as\nthe front will be moving slowly and MBE vectors are less than 10\nknots.\n\nThe front clears the southern zones on Wednesday, but could return\nnorth again on Thursday as a surface low tracks across southern\nLower Michigan.",
